 "description": "HELD VOCABULARY for procedural comprehension: the connectives, effect-verbs, role-prepositions, state/staleness markers and structural-object words a procedural passage is built from, each carried as a Concept node with a proc_role attr (and effect/slot/relation metadata). The procedural reader (domains/procedural_reader.py) recognises a token's grammatical CLASS by looking it up in THIS held table (graph-native, data-driven), not a Python literal set - the same way situation_model_reader reads its verb-frame class off seed rules and the relation-cue lexicon reads its keyword classes off seed nodes. Add a synonym by dropping a Concept here; no code changes. Every Concept is knows_concept-wired at load so seeds/intent.json's Mention -refers_to-> Concept referent rule resolves procedural mentions to these classes too.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "procedural_grammar",
  "description": "the small connective/effect grammar a read procedure is parsed against"
